    {
      "id": "7eb2adb2-bb44-451e-9048-2ddccfd323b9",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -240,
        -32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 592,
        "height": 768,
        "content": "## NDA Review & Approval - V1\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow monitors a Google Drive incoming folder for NDA files, validates that each file is supported, then moves valid files into a processing folder for text extraction. It uses OpenAI to extract NDA clauses, compares them against a Google Sheets playbook, applies deterministic approval rules, and routes the file to either an approved folder or a legal review folder. Unsupported files or extraction failures are logged separately for audit purposes.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure Google Drive credentials and set the incoming, processing, approved, and legal review folder IDs in the relevant Google Drive nodes.\n- Configure Google Sheets credentials and connect the playbook sheet plus the audit log sheets for errors, auto approvals, and legal reviews.\n- Configure OpenAI credentials for the clause extraction and playbook comparison nodes.\n- Configure the email sending credentials and recipient settings for legal review notifications.\n- Review the code nodes to ensure file type rules, extracted metadata, decision thresholds, and audit fields match the organization’s NDA review policy.\n\n### Customization\n\nCustomize the playbook sheet, deterministic rule logic, supported file types, approval thresholds, folder destinations, and legal review email recipients to match the legal team’s process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
